; Hints.inix -- what each control in a DbDo dialog does, in one sentence, spoken by Shift+F1.
; A section is a dialog's title as its window shows it; a key is a control's name, without its
; underline letter or trailing colon; add the kind in parentheses, as in "Search (Button)", only when
; two controls of one dialog share a name. [All dialogs] holds names that mean the same everywhere.
; A control with no hint here says the first sentence of its own description instead.
; Your own copy, in %LOCALAPPDATA%\DbDo\configs, wins over this one, so you can change a hint.

[All dialogs]
OK = Saves what you have chosen and closes the dialog; Control+Enter does this from any control.
Cancel = Closes the dialog and changes nothing; Escape does this from any control.
Help = Opens this dialog's help, which F1 also does from any control.
Close = Closes this window.
Records = The table's records, one to a row; arrows move by record and by column, and Enter opens the record.

[Select Columns]
Look columns = Shows look's columns in look's order, the default the table opens with; with no look, every main column.
Prime columns = Shows prime's columns in prime's order: the default sort order, and together the values unique to each record.
Main columns = Shows only the columns about the table's subject, leaving out url, tags, notes and the other standard columns.
Standard columns = Shows only the standard columns: url, tags, notes, marked, look, prime, added, edited and the id.
All columns = Shows every column of the table.
Choose columns = Lets you pick the columns one by one, in the order they should appear.
Type columns = Lets you type the column names, separated by commas, in the order they should appear.
